# Golden watchlist-review cases (obviously fictional). ONE synthetic estate: the inputs live in
# `adapters/local/_fixtures.py`, which the local adapters, the demo and this dataset all read, and
# `tests/unit/test_golden_dataset.py` holds the descriptive fields below equal to those fixtures so
# the two cannot drift into looking alike while failing differently.
#
# The eval drives the REAL service over the local adapters and scores every metric named in
# `THRESHOLDS`. The ones that score the engine sit at 1.00 because they score a pure function
# against hand-written fixtures: anything below is a defect rather than drift. `expected_floors` is
# compared as an exact SET, because a grade-only metric passes a case that reached the right answer
# for the wrong reason. Every expectation field below is read by a metric: a field nothing reads is
# documentation that goes wrong silently, which `expected_composite` and
# `expected_requires_human_review` both did.
#
# `planted` is a raw identifier deliberately embedded in the evidence; the redact-before-anything
# step must mask it, so pii_safety goes red if any raw identifier survives into an audit record.
# NRIC values must be checksum-valid or the validator will not mask them.
